<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Wu of Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 690 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Xiong Tong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Wu of Chu, personal name Xiong Tong, ruled the State of Chu from 740 to 690 BCE. In 704 BCE he became the first ruler of Chu to take the title of king, rejecting the Zhou order in which only the Zhou ruler was king. He expanded Chu against its neighbours in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> region, notably the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>, and died while on campaign against Sui in 690 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-wu-of-chu.jpg" alt="King Wu of Chu" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gu Kaizhi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chu_Wuwang_and_Deng_Man.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
